## Usage

Both map components consume a GeoJSON `FeatureCollection` (the package ships no geo data — bring your own). The default projection is Mercator clamped at ±85.05° latitude, with a display window that crops the empty poles so land fills the container. Container height defaults to the projected window's aspect ratio; pass `height` for a fixed pixel height. Data uses the accessor pattern: a key or `(row) => value` both work.

### Bubble map

Click a bubble to select its original data row, even with `roam` enabled. Drag the land to pan; scrolling over the map zooms it. Point labels render as text, not HTML.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="MapsBubbleMapDemo" code-lang="vue" title="BubbleMap + roam" description="Bubble area is proportional to value; roam enables wheel zoom and drag pan."}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxBubbleMap
      :geo-json="world"
      :data="colos"
      lng="lon"
      lat="lat"
      value="requests"
      name="city"
      roam
      :value-format="(v) => `${v.toLocaleString()} req/s`"
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### Choropleth map

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="MapsChoroplethDemo" code-lang="vue" title="ChoroplethMap + legend" description="Continuous shading interpolates by value; regions without data keep the land fill."}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxChoroplethMap
      :geo-json="world"
      :data="data"
      name="country"
      value="share"
      show-legend
      :value-format="(v) => `${v}%`"
